# Get Started with Orvi

[blue bold] Orvi is a strict, human-writable markup language: Markdown-simple text, plus native visual scopes, layout components, and semantic elements — and no HTML fallback. []

## Write it like Markdown

Headings, **bold**, _italic_, ~~strikethrough~~, lists, tables, and fenced code blocks all behave the way you expect. When you need more than text, Orvi gives you a clean path forward instead of raw tags.

## Add visual scope

Open a scope with a bracketed modifier and close it with an empty bracket:

```orvi
[green bold] looks good [] [bg=yellow] highlighted [] [lg] bigger []
```

Modifiers cover colors, sizes from xs to 2xl, weights, and a bg= background.

## Add layout and structure

[grid 2]
  ## Components
  - callout — notes and alerts, with a type
  - grid N — columns split by ---
  - card — a panel, optionally with a bg
  - tabs and tab — labelled sections
  ---
  ## Semantic lines
  - btn: Label -> url
  - img: ./picture.png | alt text
  - badge: Text | type=info
  - hr: and br:
[/grid]

[callout type=info]
  Every supported construct is expressed natively in Orvi. One strict spec, one canonical parser — no dialects to reconcile.
[/callout]

## Try it now

[grid 3]
  ## Playground
  Edit Orvi with a live preview in the browser — nothing to install.
  ---
  ## VS Code
  Install the Orvi Language extension for highlighting, diagnostics, completions, and a preview panel.
  ---
  ## Spec
  Read orvi-spec-v0.1.md for the full grammar and component reference.
[/grid]

